Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 06:16:23 -0400
Subject: pins: Arc's pinned-tab lifecycle -- a home URL, Cmd-W sleeps, the
 favicon resets

Both pin tiers record a home URL at pin time and write it to the session
(docs/features/pins.md H1, H2). Cmd-W on a pinned tab puts it to sleep
instead of closing it, under a setting (H3, H9). A pin that navigated away
shows a dot on its favicon; a click on the favicon (Option-click on an
essentials card) loads home again, and the menu offers Reset to Pinned Page
and Make This the Pinned Page (H4-H6). Peek reads the stored home's site, so
a drifted pin stops peeking the wrong site (H7).

Why: docs/ROUND6-PLAN.md wave 2 (R6-16): the pinned-tab model Arc users rely
on -- a pin is a place, not a page.
Removable when: Chromium's pinned tabs remember a home and sleep on close.
